WEBVTT

00:00:00.167 --> 00:00:01.042
Previously on The O.C.:

00:00:01.251 --> 00:00:02.627
My dad is in real-estate development.

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:04.086
You guys built the mall?

00:00:05.003 --> 00:00:06.838
I'm in charge of residential development.

00:00:07.046 --> 00:00:09.881
- Ryan and I aren't here together.
- We're done.

00:00:10.048 --> 00:00:12.049
Go after her, tell her how you feel.
It's easy.

00:00:12.258 --> 00:00:13.884
Do you want to do something tonight?

00:00:14.092 --> 00:00:15.343
I'm taking you with me.

00:00:15.551 --> 00:00:18.678
You can start over.
You can start a new life.

00:00:18.887 --> 00:00:21.388
Or I see you and the girls
in about eight to 10 years.

00:00:21.597 --> 00:00:22.973
Who's the bitch?

00:00:23.181 --> 00:00:24.891
Call an ambulance, somebody!

00:00:26.517 --> 00:00:27.726
You're gonna be okay.

00:00:31.853 --> 00:00:35.606
Are we worried your dad won't love us
if we don't feed him enough?

00:00:35.814 --> 00:00:38.482
All right. Starting now,
no more digs at my dad.

00:00:38.691 --> 00:00:40.567
Honey, that wasn't a dig. Seth?

00:00:40.817 --> 00:00:44.069
No. When you called him
a heartless bastard, that was a dig.

00:00:44.278 --> 00:00:46.487
You sold me out.

00:00:48.322 --> 00:00:51.157
See, they're like puppets
and I'm the puppet master.

00:00:51.324 --> 00:00:53.617
World domination to follow.

00:00:53.825 --> 00:00:57.161
Maybe you guys can make peace
this weekend.

00:00:57.369 --> 00:00:58.745
Okay.

00:00:58.912 --> 00:01:01.664
Oh, no, wait. We can't.

00:01:01.872 --> 00:01:04.415
- Why?
- I'm still Jewish.

00:01:04.624 --> 00:01:07.792
Just getting it out of my system,
I promise.

00:01:08.251 --> 00:01:12.170
- I wonder what his new girlfriend's like.
- I am sure she is very well-paid.

00:01:13.171 --> 00:01:15.422
I am on fire.

00:01:15.631 --> 00:01:17.340
Look at you, you're wired.

00:01:17.548 --> 00:01:20.342
Seeing your parents should make
you feel guilt, not terror.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:22.593
Don't forget, I'm also her boss.

00:01:22.802 --> 00:01:23.969
Dad.

00:01:24.178 --> 00:01:28.680
Speak of the devil, and the devil,
he doth appear. Shalom, Sandy.

00:01:29.639 --> 00:01:31.849
- How long have you been here?
- Not long.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:34.559
The Learjet got here quick.
I used my key to get in.

00:01:34.768 --> 00:01:36.602
So, Caleb, where's your new girlfriend?

00:01:36.811 --> 00:01:39.562
She's taking a swim.
Where's my grandson?

00:01:40.188 --> 00:01:43.898
So your grandpa,
he basically owns Newport, right?

00:01:44.107 --> 00:01:48.234
Yes. And, like you, he comes from humble
beginnings. You'll probably hit it off.

00:01:48.443 --> 00:01:50.152
I burned down one of his homes.

00:01:50.361 --> 00:01:54.405
But it was an accident. He owns a million
of them. It's not even on his radar.

00:01:54.613 --> 00:01:57.365
Hey, seriously, do not worry about it.
Okay, look.

00:01:57.573 --> 00:02:01.618
He lets Mom run the company, he's got
a brand-new girlfriend, he's very mellow.

00:02:01.784 --> 00:02:03.244
- Seth.
- Hey.

00:02:03.452 --> 00:02:05.036
Hey.

00:02:05.745 --> 00:02:07.163
How you doing?

00:02:07.371 --> 00:02:09.414
You're still not a football player.

00:02:09.623 --> 00:02:13.458
Yes. No. But thank you.
Grandpa, meet my friend Ryan.

00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:16.168
This is the kid that
burned down my house.

00:02:16.377 --> 00:02:18.211
Come on.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.171
So you gotta see my pictures
from Spain.

00:02:20.379 --> 00:02:24.507
And you've got to promise me to go
to Barcelona while you're still young.

00:02:24.715 --> 00:02:27.926
You wanna take those
and put them around by the grill?

00:02:28.134 --> 00:02:29.593
Hey.

00:03:04.282 --> 00:03:06.783
- Hi.
- Hi.

00:03:06.992 --> 00:03:08.535
I'm Gabrielle.

00:03:09.702 --> 00:03:10.911
I'm with Caleb.

00:03:15.664 --> 00:03:19.333
Oh, my God,
that could be my grandma.

00:04:04.028 --> 00:04:07.780
Is it twisted to find
my potential grandma really hot?

00:04:08.572 --> 00:04:11.199
Not when she looks like that.

00:04:11.365 --> 00:04:13.158
- Gabrielle.
- Yeah?

00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:16.118
We're gonna sit, drink some wine,
catch up.

00:04:16.285 --> 00:04:17.870
Okay. Do you want me to...?

00:04:18.078 --> 00:04:22.331
Hang out in the sun. Get some color.
Try to stay out of trouble.

00:04:24.749 --> 00:04:26.917
Can I join you guys?

00:04:27.125 --> 00:04:29.502
- Yeah. No...
- Yeah, come on...

00:04:34.171 --> 00:04:35.756
It's warm.

00:04:39.174 --> 00:04:41.092
So, what's up?

00:04:41.301 --> 00:04:44.136
- We were... We were talking about the...
- You were...

00:04:44.303 --> 00:04:46.221
He was telling me about the thing.

00:04:46.429 --> 00:04:50.223
So this birthday party for Caleb,
it's, like, a who's who of Newport?

00:04:50.432 --> 00:04:52.349
Should be wild, huh?

00:04:53.934 --> 00:04:57.811
- I'm being sarcastic.
- We don't get a lot of that around here.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.395
So who are you guys bringing?

00:04:59.604 --> 00:05:01.897
- I would say no one, really.
- Yeah. The same.

00:05:02.105 --> 00:05:05.524
You're kidding, right?
There are no girls you wanna bring?

00:05:05.733 --> 00:05:07.692
Two young, hot guys like yourselves?

00:05:08.401 --> 00:05:10.402
- Are you still being sarcastic?
- No.

00:05:10.611 --> 00:05:14.363
- Her name is Summer.
- And? Did you invite her yet?

00:05:14.572 --> 00:05:18.032
- It's not that simple, I mean...
- She can't say yes if you don't ask her.

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:20.992
That is very wise, Gabby.

00:05:21.659 --> 00:05:24.036
- What about you?
- Did you ask Marissa?

00:05:24.244 --> 00:05:26.662
I haven't talked to her.
I don't think she'll want to.

00:05:26.871 --> 00:05:28.705
And why not?

00:05:28.914 --> 00:05:32.458
Her family's kind of falling apart...

00:05:32.625 --> 00:05:36.002
...she's got this boyfriend she may be
back with. It's a long story.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:38.795
- They've been going out since fifth grade.
- Fifth grade?

00:05:39.004 --> 00:05:43.048
Okay, she needs to change it up. She's
known that guy since he was eating paste.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:45.883
I think he still does.

00:05:49.844 --> 00:05:51.845
Hey, babe. You decent?

00:05:52.053 --> 00:05:54.180
Hey. What are you doing here?

00:05:54.388 --> 00:05:57.849
I just came from the doctor's,
got my stitches out.

00:05:58.057 --> 00:05:59.600
Thought we could hit the beach.

00:05:59.767 --> 00:06:03.060
Don't you think it's too soon?
You should probably go home and rest.

00:06:03.269 --> 00:06:06.354
No, no. That's all I've been doing.

00:06:06.562 --> 00:06:08.355
Luke, you got shot.

00:06:08.564 --> 00:06:10.023
Yeah, I know.

00:06:13.567 --> 00:06:16.360
I know how lucky I am
to have a second chance.

00:06:16.527 --> 00:06:19.529
That's why I don't wanna
waste any more time.

00:06:20.988 --> 00:06:22.614
What do you mean?

00:06:30.411 --> 00:06:34.288
I've been an idiot. I never should have
broken up with you in the first place.

00:06:34.497 --> 00:06:36.998
And now, with everything
that's going on with your dad...

00:06:37.207 --> 00:06:40.208
The thing is, you were there for me
when I was in the hospital.

00:06:40.417 --> 00:06:43.169
And now I wanna be here for you.

00:06:49.047 --> 00:06:50.840
It's all just been so crazy.

00:06:51.049 --> 00:06:54.342
I just wish we could be together,
like it was.

00:06:58.220 --> 00:07:01.430
I... I don't know.

00:07:03.556 --> 00:07:06.308
You don't have to.
I mean, we can take it slow.

00:07:09.769 --> 00:07:12.979
Tell you what.
Let's just hang out here today.

00:07:13.187 --> 00:07:17.315
We'll sit by the pool or
watch a movie or something.

00:07:18.232 --> 00:07:20.275
Whatever you want.

00:07:21.693 --> 00:07:23.152
Okay.

00:07:30.198 --> 00:07:32.575
Gabrielle, she seems...

00:07:32.783 --> 00:07:34.701
She's 24.

00:07:34.909 --> 00:07:36.369
I'm sorry?

00:07:36.577 --> 00:07:39.370
Oh, she seems so mature for her age.

00:07:40.454 --> 00:07:43.206
These birthday festivities,
we're keeping them small, right?

00:07:43.373 --> 00:07:47.834
- It depends what you mean by "small."
- Just the family, the four of us. Gabrielle.

00:07:48.043 --> 00:07:50.044
Right. The four of us.

00:07:50.252 --> 00:07:53.421
Gabrielle, Ryan
and 150 of your closest friends.

00:07:53.629 --> 00:07:56.798
Cal, she's been working overtime on this.
The menus, the invitations.

00:07:57.006 --> 00:07:58.799
On top of all her other work.

00:07:59.008 --> 00:08:01.009
- Is it too much?
- No. Work is great.

00:08:01.217 --> 00:08:04.928
- The new development's back on track.
- After your boy nearly burned it down.

00:08:05.762 --> 00:08:09.097
We've had setbacks, but the insurance
more than covered the damages.

00:08:09.306 --> 00:08:13.767
I hear you've commissioned an architect
I've never approved to do the redesign.

00:08:13.975 --> 00:08:16.727
Yes, but I would never build
without consulting you.

00:08:16.894 --> 00:08:19.187
Honey, you don't need my approval.

00:08:19.771 --> 00:08:22.939
After all, you adopted the boy
without consulting me.

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:28.985
I would have called you about Ryan,
but there wasn't enough time.

00:08:29.193 --> 00:08:32.487
I'm pushing you too hard.
Things are slipping through the cracks.

00:08:32.695 --> 00:08:36.906
Which is why I've decided to
scale back your responsibilities.

00:08:37.115 --> 00:08:39.950
- You're demoting me?
- I wanna get more involved.

00:08:40.158 --> 00:08:43.952
Give you a chance to spend a bit more
time with your new family, your new son.

00:08:44.161 --> 00:08:47.621
Now, then.
Tell me all about Jimmy Cooper.

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:50.040
Son of a bitch lost $4 million?

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:59.170
I took Kaitlin by the stables
to say goodbye to China.

00:08:59.796 --> 00:09:02.089
Guess she won't be
needing these anymore.

00:09:04.799 --> 00:09:07.467
You know, I think China
was her best friend.

00:09:07.634 --> 00:09:10.302
- China's a horse.
- Maybe to you.

00:09:10.511 --> 00:09:12.637
Hey, you know...

00:09:13.137 --> 00:09:16.181
- I don't feel good about this.
- Well, you shouldn't.

00:09:16.389 --> 00:09:20.976
What do you...?
What do you want from me?

00:09:24.811 --> 00:09:26.437
I think I want a divorce.

00:09:35.109 --> 00:09:37.861
I'm sorry, honey.

00:09:38.028 --> 00:09:40.196
I just don't see any other way.

00:09:48.159 --> 00:09:51.119
- Hey.
- I was on my way to work.

00:09:51.328 --> 00:09:53.704
- We hadn't talked in a while.
- I was gonna call you.

00:09:53.913 --> 00:09:57.957
No, it's cool. So Kirsten's dad's
in town, they're having this...

00:09:58.124 --> 00:09:59.666
Hey.

00:10:01.292 --> 00:10:03.586
- Hi.
- Hey, how you doing, man?

00:10:03.794 --> 00:10:05.337
Fine.

00:10:05.503 --> 00:10:11.424
Yeah, I never got a chance to
thank you for taking me to the hospital...

00:10:11.632 --> 00:10:13.925
...and giving Marissa a call.

00:10:16.886 --> 00:10:18.928
Yeah, no problem.

00:10:19.137 --> 00:10:22.055
Do you have some aspirin?
My arm's killing me from the stitches.

00:10:22.264 --> 00:10:27.309
- Yeah, check in my parents' bathroom.
- All right, thanks. Hey, take it easy, guy.

00:10:31.603 --> 00:10:33.062
So, what's going on?

00:10:34.688 --> 00:10:38.024
I was gonna see if you wanted to...

00:10:39.024 --> 00:10:40.609
I was gonna see how you were doing.

00:10:40.817 --> 00:10:43.277
You seem to be doing good...

00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:46.904
...so I'm gonna get to work. Later.

00:10:57.494 --> 00:10:59.037
Hey.

00:11:00.121 --> 00:11:01.830
Hi.

00:11:02.039 --> 00:11:03.915
Seth and Caleb are sailing.

00:11:04.957 --> 00:11:08.710
I've never seen two people
more excited about boats.

00:11:11.128 --> 00:11:14.380
Seth said you worked here,
and I could use a cocktail.

00:11:17.382 --> 00:11:20.884
- I can't serve you.
- Right. You're not legal.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:26.054
- How about a cranberry juice?
- That I can do.

00:11:28.305 --> 00:11:31.724
From the flight. I hate flying.

00:11:31.932 --> 00:11:35.768
- You?
- I've never been on a plane.

00:11:37.102 --> 00:11:38.687
My first time, I was 15.

00:11:38.895 --> 00:11:42.064
My mother sent me to Japan
all by myself to do some modeling.

00:11:42.647 --> 00:11:45.399
She figured it was easier
than her having to get a job.

00:11:45.608 --> 00:11:48.484
- I can relate.
- I've heard.

00:11:52.612 --> 00:11:54.905
So how'd the modeling thing turn out?

00:11:55.114 --> 00:11:59.033
Well, when you're a teenager and you're
living in a house with a bunch of girls...

00:11:59.241 --> 00:12:02.326
...with no parents,
things can get a little insane.

00:12:04.078 --> 00:12:07.705
By the time I got clean, I was 22,
retirement age.

00:12:13.417 --> 00:12:17.211
You must think it's weird,
me with an older guy.

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:21.213
I live in a pool house.

00:12:25.383 --> 00:12:27.842
So how did it work out with your girl?

00:12:28.801 --> 00:12:31.345
- Paste-eater?
- They have a past.

00:12:31.970 --> 00:12:33.763
Excuse me? More water.

00:12:43.852 --> 00:12:46.062
Oh, Kirsten, come on, honey.

00:12:46.271 --> 00:12:49.356
You could not have
done more or done better.

00:12:49.564 --> 00:12:53.358
I just don't understand. I've worked
so hard for him. I've killed myself for him.

00:12:53.567 --> 00:12:58.528
Well, the man is a bottomless pit of need.
You think you can fill it? You can't.

00:13:02.322 --> 00:13:04.615
You're amazing.

00:13:04.824 --> 00:13:07.075
If he can't appreciate you, screw him.

00:13:07.284 --> 00:13:09.952
Quit. Quit.

00:13:10.161 --> 00:13:13.871
You've never supported me working
for him. You've never liked him.

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:17.999
You're right. Not since our wedding day,
when you walked yourself down the aisle.

00:13:18.207 --> 00:13:20.334
He was in Singapore.
There was a monsoon.

00:13:20.542 --> 00:13:23.002
Baby, we changed the date three times
for his schedule.

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:25.712
He makes the world revolve around him,
including you.

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:27.922
Sandy, he's my dad.

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:31.507
He's ruining your life. Quit.

00:13:33.759 --> 00:13:35.676
I can't.

00:13:38.553 --> 00:13:42.931
So you're living in a pool house.
And then? So, what's next for you?

00:13:43.139 --> 00:13:45.891
What's next for you?
Learjet to London, Paris in the fall?

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:47.350
Perhaps.

00:13:50.436 --> 00:13:52.312
I'll be right back.

00:13:55.439 --> 00:13:57.148
- Hi.
- Hey.

00:13:57.857 --> 00:13:59.024
Got a minute?

00:14:05.487 --> 00:14:07.154
What's up?

00:14:07.822 --> 00:14:12.033
- I wanted to talk to you before, but...
- Luke was there.

00:14:12.199 --> 00:14:13.742
Right.

00:14:19.204 --> 00:14:21.538
He wants to get back together.

00:14:22.873 --> 00:14:27.000
- What did you tell him?
- I told him I needed to think about it.

00:14:33.129 --> 00:14:34.463
I don't know what I should do.

00:14:37.882 --> 00:14:39.967
I don't know either.

00:14:40.926 --> 00:14:42.135
I know. I just...

00:14:42.343 --> 00:14:44.803
Look, if you came here for me
to help you choose...

00:14:45.011 --> 00:14:47.972
- Of course not...
- Good.

00:14:51.641 --> 00:14:55.977
Why don't you just let me know
when you've made up your mind. Okay?

00:15:01.772 --> 00:15:03.315
Okay.

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:17.407
If he'd just said something.
I mean, I just wanted him to say anything.

00:15:17.615 --> 00:15:19.533
Well, you can't expect him
to choose, Coop.

00:15:19.742 --> 00:15:22.785
He comes from a place where they have
knife fights, drag racing...

00:15:22.994 --> 00:15:26.120
...and sex on the hood of a car.
- That's from Fast and the Furious.

00:15:26.329 --> 00:15:29.164
- That movie was based on a true story.
- No, it wasn't.

00:15:29.331 --> 00:15:33.292
Whatevs. All I'm saying is you have
to do the choosing, not him or Luke.

00:15:49.177 --> 00:15:52.137
It's fate. It's destiny.
Look, we both like burritos.

00:15:52.345 --> 00:15:54.388
You wanna eat somewhere else?

00:15:54.597 --> 00:15:57.348
Who's winning right now,
me or my hair?

00:16:01.809 --> 00:16:03.727
I'm gonna get us some salsa.

00:16:05.729 --> 00:16:07.938
Hi, Summer.

00:16:08.147 --> 00:16:09.856
Seth Cohen.

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:14.276
Could you give me a hand...

00:16:14.484 --> 00:16:16.527
...over here?

00:16:24.157 --> 00:16:25.908
Okay.

00:16:26.116 --> 00:16:29.118
I... I know you gotta figure
some stuff out. I get that.

00:16:29.327 --> 00:16:33.955
But in the meantime, there's this party
at... Well, it's for Seth's grandfather.

00:16:34.163 --> 00:16:36.123
I know. I'm going.

00:16:36.331 --> 00:16:38.457
Luke asked me this morning.

00:16:42.293 --> 00:16:47.129
Cool. Well, I'll see
you and Luke tomorrow, then.

00:16:50.215 --> 00:16:52.174
Yeah. See you.

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:56.635
Two salsa verdes. Aggressive.

00:16:56.802 --> 00:16:58.887
Pico de gallo, that's a classic.

00:16:59.095 --> 00:17:02.014
Holy jalape Ío. Somebody came to play.

00:17:02.222 --> 00:17:04.974
Are there any napkins?

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:08.059
No.

00:17:08.268 --> 00:17:10.227
- Lick it.
- What?

00:17:10.436 --> 00:17:12.770
I just got my nails done.
It'll ruin the polish.

00:17:12.979 --> 00:17:16.940
- You lick it.
- I don't like picante. It's for Marissa.

00:17:22.235 --> 00:17:23.777
- Thanks.
- It's good.

00:17:23.944 --> 00:17:26.904
Now, aren't you gonna invite me
to your grandpa's party?

00:17:28.405 --> 00:17:30.532
I'm sorry, Summer,
could you please repeat that?

00:17:30.740 --> 00:17:34.242
Your grandpa's having this
awesome party. It's at your house.

00:17:34.451 --> 00:17:36.869
And I thought we were friends.

00:17:37.077 --> 00:17:40.621
Wait a second. Do you want me to ask
you because you wanna go with me...

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:43.957
...or just because you wanna go?

00:17:44.248 --> 00:17:46.041
Fair enough. I'll see you at 8.

00:17:47.125 --> 00:17:49.794
- Hey.
- Hey. How was court?

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:53.754
I was distracted all day. I was thinking,
if you quit, know what we could do?

00:17:53.963 --> 00:17:55.756
- I'm not quitting.
- Hear me out.

00:17:55.964 --> 00:17:58.799
We could buy back our old house
in Berkeley.

00:17:59.008 --> 00:18:01.092
You loved that house.
Seth loved that house.

00:18:01.301 --> 00:18:03.511
That house had bad plumbing
and termites.

00:18:03.719 --> 00:18:05.845
It was a fixer-upper we never got
to fix up.

00:18:06.054 --> 00:18:07.054
I know.

00:18:07.263 --> 00:18:10.557
We moved here because your mom
got sick. We never planned to stay.

00:18:10.765 --> 00:18:14.434
If you quit, we could do anything
we want. We could go anywhere.

00:18:14.642 --> 00:18:16.227
No, we can't.

00:18:16.435 --> 00:18:20.896
Why not? Seth has been planning
his exodus from this place since he was 6.

00:18:21.105 --> 00:18:22.397
Ryan wouldn't care.

00:18:22.606 --> 00:18:25.900
You could get that little gallery
in Sausalito you've always dreamed of.

00:18:26.108 --> 00:18:28.943
Or the Mission. You could put
your art history degree to use.

00:18:29.152 --> 00:18:31.069
I haven't thought about
that gallery in years.

00:18:31.278 --> 00:18:33.071
So...

00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:36.156
...think about it.

00:18:38.282 --> 00:18:39.742
Think about it.

00:18:39.908 --> 00:18:42.910
Is this too slutty to wear
to an old guy's birthday party?

00:18:43.119 --> 00:18:44.870
I don't want the dude
to have a coronary.

00:18:45.078 --> 00:18:47.496
I can't believe
you're actually going with Seth.

00:18:47.705 --> 00:18:51.749
Aloha? Caleb Nichol is, like,
the Donald Trump of the West.

00:18:51.916 --> 00:18:53.375
Do you know how many hot, rich...

00:18:53.583 --> 00:18:56.710
...twenty-something banker-brokers
are gonna be there?

00:18:56.919 --> 00:18:59.837
A lot. And now I have someone
to introduce me to them.

00:19:00.046 --> 00:19:02.798
- Isn't that a little mean to Seth?
- To who?

00:19:04.048 --> 00:19:05.591
Kidding.

00:19:07.259 --> 00:19:08.968
That was delicious, Kirsten.

00:19:09.177 --> 00:19:11.386
Well, thank you.
I order from them all the time.

00:19:11.595 --> 00:19:13.679
Less time at work,
more time for cooking.

00:19:13.888 --> 00:19:17.390
Because there's no place Kirsten feels
more comfortable than in the kitchen.

00:19:17.598 --> 00:19:20.350
- What? Mom can't even make cereal.
- Thanks, Seth.

00:19:20.517 --> 00:19:22.852
- I love you, Mom.
- I love you too.

00:19:23.602 --> 00:19:27.188
You have a quick wit, Seth.
Amazing you're not better at skirt-chasing.

00:19:29.814 --> 00:19:34.609
Well, if by "skirts" you mean girls,
in your outdated cowboy-speak...

00:19:34.818 --> 00:19:38.695
...I have a little news for you. Turns out
somebody has a date to your party.

00:19:40.738 --> 00:19:45.032
And it's not a big deal or anything,
but if you must know, Summer asked me.

00:19:45.241 --> 00:19:49.827
- Summer. Summer's hot.
- You did not just say that.

00:19:50.035 --> 00:19:52.704
- Say what?
- Just go, please.

00:19:52.871 --> 00:19:54.497
You go.

00:19:57.540 --> 00:19:59.500
What about you, Ryan?

00:20:02.918 --> 00:20:05.462
Nope. Going by myself.

00:20:17.844 --> 00:20:21.472
Caleb seems to be in good spirits.
He just finished a second bottle of merlot.

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:25.349
- Now would be a good time to talk to him.
- I'm not ready for that conversation.

00:20:25.558 --> 00:20:27.184
What conversation?

00:20:27.392 --> 00:20:29.352
- Got any grappa?
- Yeah.

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:32.103
- Are you adopting another kid?
- It's nothing.

00:20:32.312 --> 00:20:35.147
- Actually, it's something.
- I've never known my daughter...

00:20:35.355 --> 00:20:38.399
...to need someone to speak for her.
- Maybe you've never gotten to know her.

00:20:38.607 --> 00:20:41.693
If you did, you'd know she's the best
thing that ever happened to your company.

00:20:41.901 --> 00:20:44.361
You'd support her,
not demote her so she wants to quit.

00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:46.738
- Is that true? You wanna quit?
- No...

00:20:46.946 --> 00:20:49.156
- Kirsten.
- We were talking...

00:20:49.364 --> 00:20:53.492
About selling this house and moving back
to Berkeley, like we'd always planned.

00:20:53.700 --> 00:20:57.411
You're not serious. You're still
smoking the weed, aren't you?

00:20:57.619 --> 00:20:59.287
- Dad...
- Dad, you smoke weed?

00:20:59.496 --> 00:21:02.664
- Out, now. Private conversation.
- Ryan, guess who's a stoner.

00:21:02.873 --> 00:21:04.582
Honey, don't be afraid of him.

00:21:04.790 --> 00:21:08.293
You keep your mouth shut.
No one here cares what you think.

00:21:08.501 --> 00:21:10.669
Don't talk to me like that
in my own house.

00:21:10.878 --> 00:21:14.505
Whose house is this? Who built it?
Who paid for it?

00:21:14.713 --> 00:21:16.464
- Dad.
- This is between you and me, Kiki.

00:21:16.673 --> 00:21:18.341
You're gonna do what you want anyway.

00:21:18.549 --> 00:21:22.260
- Should we maybe go?
- Adopting juvenile delinquents.

00:21:22.468 --> 00:21:24.178
- Maybe let's just...
- Yeah, let's.

00:21:24.386 --> 00:21:27.263
You're making a big deal of this.
It was nothing.

00:21:27.555 --> 00:21:29.681
Doesn't sound like nothing.

00:21:30.223 --> 00:21:34.768
In fact, thanks, Sandy,
for letting me know how she feels.

00:21:34.976 --> 00:21:38.645
She would never tell me that.
She never tells me anything.

00:21:38.853 --> 00:21:42.314
If you wanna quit, that's fine.
I'll expect your resignation tomorrow.

00:21:42.898 --> 00:21:44.816
Now, then. The grappa.

00:21:46.692 --> 00:21:51.737
So, Gabrielle, I heard Grandpa's taking
you on the helicopter tour tomorrow.

00:21:51.945 --> 00:21:56.489
Yeah. He wants to show me
his Orange County empire.

00:21:56.698 --> 00:22:00.075
- This game sucks.
- Let me see it.

00:22:03.452 --> 00:22:05.954
Ryan, you've been playing
the pirate game?

00:22:06.162 --> 00:22:08.163
That's a little bit minty.

00:22:08.372 --> 00:22:11.707
- What else do you have?
- I'll go get you "Pro Skater 3." It's good.

00:22:12.666 --> 00:22:16.127
Hey. We gotta go searching
for my dad's bong later, all right?

00:22:20.088 --> 00:22:21.630
So...

00:22:22.589 --> 00:22:25.633
...does he always yell like that?
- Pretty much.

00:22:25.841 --> 00:22:30.719
He's the boss, and every relationship
is a business relationship to him.

00:22:31.261 --> 00:22:32.971
Even yours?

00:22:34.680 --> 00:22:36.973
He'll only ever really love one woman.

00:22:37.182 --> 00:22:40.309
And she passed away years ago.

00:22:40.851 --> 00:22:43.310
For now, he's just looking
to stay entertained...

00:22:43.811 --> 00:22:46.479
...keep from being bored.

00:22:47.396 --> 00:22:48.772
But aren't we all?

00:22:58.612 --> 00:23:00.780
I am so bored.

00:23:04.657 --> 00:23:07.117
- Do you think...?
- Don't think.

00:23:20.834 --> 00:23:22.376
Gabrielle.

00:23:22.585 --> 00:23:24.753
We're leaving. Now.

00:23:32.550 --> 00:23:34.551
Back to the office.

00:23:51.645 --> 00:23:54.980
- How's Gabrielle?
- I don't know.

00:23:55.189 --> 00:23:56.981
Oh, really?

00:23:57.190 --> 00:24:00.942
Okay, Ryan, let me present
exhibit A to you.

00:24:01.151 --> 00:24:04.069
She opted to forgo sailing
to go to the Crab Shack?

00:24:04.653 --> 00:24:06.446
So? Not everyone likes sailing.

00:24:07.655 --> 00:24:10.156
Okay. Let's take it to exhibit B here.

00:24:10.365 --> 00:24:14.909
Intense, some would even say smoldering,
eye contact at the table.

00:24:15.118 --> 00:24:17.911
She was mad-dogging you.
And finally, the clincher...

00:24:18.120 --> 00:24:20.663
...last night in the pool house,
she chose to sit on your bed...

00:24:20.871 --> 00:24:22.706
...even though there was an empty chair.

00:24:22.914 --> 00:24:26.583
Come on, boys, out of the pool.
Caterers are here. Time to get ready.

00:24:27.459 --> 00:24:29.543
I would like some answers.

00:24:30.502 --> 00:24:32.504
Yeah, okay, we hooked up.

00:24:33.171 --> 00:24:35.839
- What?
- Isn't that what you were asking?

00:24:36.006 --> 00:24:39.883
I noticed some heavy flirting, yes...

00:24:40.092 --> 00:24:41.759
You hooked up with my grandma?

00:24:44.094 --> 00:24:48.138
- Actually, that's kind of hot. How was it?
- No one can know about this.

00:24:48.305 --> 00:24:50.348
I agree completely. How was it?

00:24:50.557 --> 00:24:52.266
It was good.

00:24:52.975 --> 00:24:55.518
Weird, but good.

00:24:58.603 --> 00:25:02.773
- What about Marissa?
- What about her?

00:25:09.777 --> 00:25:12.904
'73 Dom. Yes, that's his favorite.
Thank you.

00:25:17.740 --> 00:25:19.408
Is there cilantro in that?

00:25:19.616 --> 00:25:21.076
Great, he hates it.

00:25:22.618 --> 00:25:24.911
I can't believe
you still went through with this.

00:25:25.120 --> 00:25:29.247
I had no choice, even though you tried
to sabotage the entire weekend.

00:25:29.456 --> 00:25:33.167
Honey, I'm sorry I jumped the gun
last night. Ready?

00:25:34.876 --> 00:25:36.335
- Hello.
- Hi.

00:25:36.544 --> 00:25:38.503
- Dad, you made it.
- How you doing?

00:25:38.712 --> 00:25:40.713
- Disappointed?
- No.

00:25:40.921 --> 00:25:43.006
- Sandy.
- Hey, happy birthday, Caleb.

00:25:43.215 --> 00:25:45.799
- Can I get you a drink?
- Absolutely.

00:25:46.925 --> 00:25:49.677
- Dad, happy birthday.
- Thanks.

00:25:49.844 --> 00:25:52.929
- Look, about the other night...
- Just forget about it.

00:25:53.096 --> 00:25:56.139
Just make sure that you let me know
when you plan to give notice...

00:25:56.348 --> 00:25:59.266
...so that I can hire your replacement.
- Caleb.

00:26:00.517 --> 00:26:02.268
Quite a party.

00:26:15.777 --> 00:26:17.819
You look...

00:26:30.035 --> 00:26:32.078
You clean up good.

00:26:33.913 --> 00:26:35.997
Are you trying to get caught?

00:26:37.040 --> 00:26:38.958
Find me later.

00:26:46.296 --> 00:26:47.922
I wish Dad had come.

00:26:48.088 --> 00:26:51.132
Why, so you could break up
another brawl?

00:26:51.340 --> 00:26:53.217
Hi, how are you?

00:26:53.425 --> 00:26:54.884
Hey, Summer.

00:26:56.927 --> 00:26:59.054
You look... Yeah.

00:26:59.262 --> 00:27:01.055
Hey, Marissa. Hi, Luke.

00:27:01.263 --> 00:27:03.765
Cohen, how you doing?
It's good to see you.

00:27:03.973 --> 00:27:07.517
- It is?
- So this is your place. It's beautiful.

00:27:07.726 --> 00:27:10.019
- Thank you.
- Mariss, something to drink?

00:27:10.227 --> 00:27:11.395
Sure.

00:27:13.438 --> 00:27:15.939
Okay, he got shot in the arm,
not the head.

00:27:16.148 --> 00:27:18.691
Come on.
Don't you wanna show me off?

00:27:27.780 --> 00:27:30.532
I'm in private equity
and portfolio management.

00:27:30.740 --> 00:27:33.659
Really? Private equity
and portfolio management.

00:27:33.825 --> 00:27:36.577
Sounds fascinating.

00:27:43.581 --> 00:27:46.833
It's a great party. Everybody seems
to be having a good time.

00:27:47.042 --> 00:27:48.585
Almost everybody.

00:27:48.751 --> 00:27:51.044
Look. Look, I...

00:27:51.253 --> 00:27:55.005
I wish I could tell you I'm sorry,
but I'm not.

00:27:55.214 --> 00:27:58.216
- Okay, worst apology ever.
- You know I'm no good at those.

00:27:58.382 --> 00:28:01.676
Look, the important thing is,
it's out there. You spoke your mind.

00:28:01.885 --> 00:28:03.844
No. You spoke my mind.

00:28:04.053 --> 00:28:08.347
I thought we had an understanding.
I thought this was what we both wanted.

00:28:08.555 --> 00:28:10.640
It is. It was.

00:28:10.848 --> 00:28:13.350
You're backing down.
He's been doing this to you for years.

00:28:13.558 --> 00:28:16.519
My dad isn't the reason we stayed here.

00:28:16.727 --> 00:28:18.687
We are. We chose this.

00:28:21.063 --> 00:28:23.898
If you're telling me that all this time
you've been unhappy...

00:28:24.065 --> 00:28:26.567
...that this isn't what you want...

00:28:26.817 --> 00:28:29.610
...then this is a much bigger conversation.

00:28:36.406 --> 00:28:37.782
I've got Pilates.

00:28:37.990 --> 00:28:40.325
- How's that going?
- It's great.

00:28:41.534 --> 00:28:43.244
It's Jimmy.

00:28:45.412 --> 00:28:47.246
Excuse me.

00:28:49.831 --> 00:28:53.500
I told you not to come.
What the hell are you doing here?

00:28:53.709 --> 00:28:56.460
I've got a plan, okay? Just take it easy.

00:28:56.669 --> 00:28:58.462
A chance to go back to the way it was.

00:28:58.670 --> 00:29:02.297
- You built a time machine?
- Caleb employs thousands of people.

00:29:02.547 --> 00:29:04.173
None are more qualified than me.

00:29:04.382 --> 00:29:08.676
How big a leap can it be from investing
in stocks to investing in real estate?

00:29:08.801 --> 00:29:12.012
- You are not asking him for a job.
- Why not?

00:29:12.220 --> 00:29:14.680
This whole community thinks
you're a criminal, Jimmy.

00:29:14.888 --> 00:29:17.640
Caleb Nichol owns the community.
He'll feel the same.

00:29:17.849 --> 00:29:20.684
The guy's loved me since I was a kid.
He taught me how to sail.

00:29:20.892 --> 00:29:24.686
When I was a junior in high school, he
tried to convince me to propose to Kirsten.

00:29:24.895 --> 00:29:27.938
Please. Don't even think
of talking to him.

00:29:29.356 --> 00:29:34.859
Look, I'm sorry. But if there's a chance
that I can save this family...

00:29:35.068 --> 00:29:36.986
...I'm gonna take it.

00:29:41.947 --> 00:29:43.156
This party rocks.

00:29:43.365 --> 00:29:46.033
- I cannot believe David Manperl's here.
- Who?

00:29:46.200 --> 00:29:49.619
Senior vice president of the
wealth-management division at McKenna.

00:29:49.827 --> 00:29:51.828
You know, the venture capitalist firm.

00:29:52.037 --> 00:29:55.581
He manages wealth as a job.

00:29:55.789 --> 00:29:57.749
I've been reading Forbes.

00:29:57.957 --> 00:29:59.333
I see.

00:29:59.500 --> 00:30:02.918
So you chose Luke, huh?

00:30:03.127 --> 00:30:05.670
Chino didn't stand a chance.
I told you Luke was the one.

00:30:05.879 --> 00:30:07.255
No, you didn't.

00:30:07.463 --> 00:30:09.047
Well, I meant to.

00:30:10.256 --> 00:30:12.675
You guys are all over each other.

00:30:12.883 --> 00:30:15.551
- Did you...? Did it happen?
- No.

00:30:15.760 --> 00:30:17.344
Well, his willpower is amazing.

00:30:17.553 --> 00:30:19.887
- The fact that you two haven't had sex...
- Summer!

00:30:20.096 --> 00:30:22.014
Coop, what more do you want?

00:30:22.222 --> 00:30:26.475
He's beautiful, sweet,
totally crazy about you.

00:30:26.683 --> 00:30:28.768
What are you waiting for?

00:30:30.352 --> 00:30:32.270
I don't know.

00:30:32.479 --> 00:30:36.606
Well, you better figure it out, because
he's not gonna be able to wait forever.

00:31:03.039 --> 00:31:05.416
- What are you doing?
- Nothing.

00:31:05.624 --> 00:31:07.084
Somebody's hiding.

00:31:07.292 --> 00:31:09.210
No, I'm just...

00:31:09.418 --> 00:31:11.044
Bored.

00:31:13.629 --> 00:31:14.755
Me too.

00:31:14.964 --> 00:31:16.506
I've heard.

00:31:17.298 --> 00:31:20.634
- She's just a girl.
- I know.

00:31:23.177 --> 00:31:26.429
- So why are you hiding from her?
- I'm not.

00:31:27.138 --> 00:31:29.264
I don't believe you.

00:31:41.230 --> 00:31:43.773
- Still bored?
- Not so much.

00:32:02.035 --> 00:32:05.370
Sorry. I... I thought...

00:32:07.288 --> 00:32:08.914
Sorry.

00:32:25.466 --> 00:32:27.467
I've just been surfing...

00:32:27.676 --> 00:32:29.760
Hey, babe, I was looking...

00:32:33.096 --> 00:32:36.098
- Let's go.
- Yeah, okay.

00:32:47.104 --> 00:32:50.398
We could go to my place.
My parents went to Palm Springs.

00:32:50.607 --> 00:32:52.733
Yeah, sure. Great.

00:32:59.737 --> 00:33:04.574
Pharmaceuticals. Isn't that the
largest-growing industry in North America?

00:33:07.784 --> 00:33:10.744
Remember the old days, Jimmy?
Where's the time gone?

00:33:10.953 --> 00:33:13.788
Great to see you again, as always.

00:33:17.290 --> 00:33:21.209
Hey. Congratulations.
Looks like you got yourself a job.

00:33:21.418 --> 00:33:23.335
Oh, yeah.
Caleb couldn't have been nicer...

00:33:23.544 --> 00:33:26.045
...when he said there was no way
he could hire me.

00:33:27.922 --> 00:33:31.674
- Well, hate to say I told you so.
- No, you don't.

00:33:32.633 --> 00:33:34.676
Where are you going?

00:33:36.469 --> 00:33:38.261
To finish what you started.

00:33:42.681 --> 00:33:45.766
- Happy birthday, Cal.
- Julie. Thank you.

00:33:45.975 --> 00:33:47.892
I'll call you next week.

00:33:48.101 --> 00:33:50.853
- How are you?
- Well, I'm sure you've heard.

00:33:51.061 --> 00:33:55.272
- Kirsten's brought you up to speed.
- I'm really sorry. About everything.

00:33:55.772 --> 00:33:57.815
I really liked your husband.

00:33:58.024 --> 00:33:59.900
Soon to be ex-husband.

00:34:00.901 --> 00:34:04.736
Can't expect me to stay with him, not
after he's lied to me, left us with nothing.

00:34:05.320 --> 00:34:07.655
- Nothing?
- Yeah.

00:34:08.906 --> 00:34:11.741
I suppose I'll have to get a job now,
doing God knows what.

00:34:11.907 --> 00:34:13.950
It's not like I have
any marketable skills.

00:34:14.159 --> 00:34:15.701
Well, I'm sure that's not true.

00:34:15.910 --> 00:34:20.413
You know, if there's anything
that I can do for you or the girls...

00:34:20.621 --> 00:34:23.706
You're very, very sweet.
And very busy.

00:34:28.585 --> 00:34:30.794
I just wanted to say happy birthday.

00:34:31.003 --> 00:34:33.129
I'm never too busy for you.

00:34:33.338 --> 00:34:36.089
We'll have dinner,
figure something out.

00:34:36.298 --> 00:34:37.882
I'd like that.

00:34:39.091 --> 00:34:40.550
Thank you.

00:34:54.726 --> 00:34:57.728
Hey. What are you doing?
I need you to introduce me...

00:34:57.936 --> 00:35:01.188
- Okay. You know what, Summer? No.
- What?

00:35:01.397 --> 00:35:04.524
This whole night, all you've done
is use me to meet rich older guys.

00:35:04.899 --> 00:35:07.192
That's not true.

00:35:08.151 --> 00:35:09.860
Okay. Maybe a little.

00:35:10.069 --> 00:35:13.654
Do you have any idea how pathetic it is
to listen to you talk about mergers...

00:35:13.863 --> 00:35:16.531
...while some guy
just stares at your boobs?

00:35:16.740 --> 00:35:19.825
- Which guy was staring at my boobs?
- Who cares?

00:35:20.033 --> 00:35:24.286
The point is, if that guy doesn't know you,
he doesn't care about who you really are.

00:35:24.494 --> 00:35:27.830
He has no idea that every day
of third grade you shared your lunch...

00:35:28.038 --> 00:35:31.040
...with a skinny squirrel whose nuts
were stolen by a fat squirrel.

00:35:31.249 --> 00:35:32.458
I hated that mean squirrel.

00:35:32.666 --> 00:35:35.877
None of those guys were there
when you read your poem aloud in class...

00:35:36.085 --> 00:35:39.170
...and your hand was shaking
because you were nervous.

00:35:39.379 --> 00:35:41.672
Poem? What poem?

00:35:43.923 --> 00:35:47.342
"I Wish I Was a Mermaid."

00:35:49.302 --> 00:35:51.470
You remember that?

00:35:51.678 --> 00:35:53.804
That was, like, sixth grade.

00:35:57.390 --> 00:36:00.725
I wish I was a mermaid
And...

00:36:03.435 --> 00:36:06.771
Was friends with all the fish
A shiny tail and seashells, that's...

00:36:17.319 --> 00:36:19.862
What I would wish

00:36:26.200 --> 00:36:28.284
Oh, I gotta go.

00:36:28.493 --> 00:36:32.537
There's that investment banker
from Woodward and McDonnough.

00:36:33.913 --> 00:36:37.665
It's okay. I'll introduce myself.

00:36:46.963 --> 00:36:48.339
The greatest party ever.

00:36:51.716 --> 00:36:55.551
- She has no intention of quitting.
- Doesn't sound that way to me.

00:36:55.760 --> 00:36:59.345
Well, I wish she would,
so we could get the hell away from you.

00:36:59.554 --> 00:37:01.138
- Lf you're looking for a fight...
- Save it.

00:37:01.347 --> 00:37:05.141
We both know you're punishing her
because she's doing so well without you.

00:37:06.475 --> 00:37:10.311
You're afraid she won't need your help
to run the company or her family.

00:37:10.519 --> 00:37:12.979
And I got news for you.
She's better than you at both.

00:37:13.187 --> 00:37:16.314
If you don't wanna lose her,
let her keep doing what she's been doing.

00:37:16.523 --> 00:37:21.234
You'll stay rich, she'll be happy,
and I'll figure out a way to make it work.

00:37:22.860 --> 00:37:24.736
I need a corkscrew.

00:37:29.114 --> 00:37:30.782
Have a nice time.

00:37:44.332 --> 00:37:45.958
Great party, Kiki.

00:37:49.919 --> 00:37:51.503
Your mom would have loved it.

00:37:52.545 --> 00:37:56.298
Birthdays, holidays.
She always loved a good party.

00:37:56.506 --> 00:37:57.882
She did.

00:38:02.468 --> 00:38:03.636
I miss her.

00:38:04.845 --> 00:38:07.179
I know. Me too.

00:38:10.140 --> 00:38:13.225
Your sister, do you ever hear from her?

00:38:13.392 --> 00:38:15.893
I wanted to invite her,
but I couldn't reach her.

00:38:16.102 --> 00:38:18.311
The number I have
is no longer in service.

00:38:20.146 --> 00:38:24.982
- And then there were two.
- You could look at it like that.

00:38:28.985 --> 00:38:30.611
You're all I got, Kiki.

00:38:31.778 --> 00:38:34.863
And then I'm running you so ragged
you haven't got time to talk to me.

00:38:35.072 --> 00:38:39.783
That's not true, and you know it.
I love working for you.

00:38:41.034 --> 00:38:43.202
I just want you to be proud of me.

00:38:57.086 --> 00:38:59.337
Taking in a stray kid.

00:39:00.254 --> 00:39:02.381
That's the sort of thing your mom
would've done.

00:39:02.589 --> 00:39:05.591
Yeah, except she would have done it
just to piss you off.

00:39:15.764 --> 00:39:17.473
Don't be late Monday.

00:39:37.403 --> 00:39:39.487
- Hi.
- Hi.

00:39:43.698 --> 00:39:45.950
So I guess she likes you.

00:39:48.785 --> 00:39:50.744
I guess she did.

00:39:56.248 --> 00:39:58.916
You look so sad. I...

00:39:59.792 --> 00:40:01.584
I'd give anything to be that miserable.

00:40:05.003 --> 00:40:09.923
Because if I remember correctly,
that's what it feels like to be in love.

00:40:42.944 --> 00:40:44.778
I love you so much.

00:41:07.000 --> 00:41:08.376
Do you...?

00:41:09.627 --> 00:41:11.461
I mean, are you...?

00:41:13.212 --> 00:41:14.588
Okay.

00:41:18.007 --> 00:41:19.883
Yeah, you're sure?

00:41:21.051 --> 00:41:22.427
Yeah.

00:41:23.094 --> 00:41:24.803
I want to.

00:41:26.763 --> 00:41:28.722
Should I grab a...?

00:41:30.140 --> 00:41:31.432
Yeah.

00:42:16.085 --> 00:42:19.212
- Do you want me to walk you in?
- No. Thanks.

00:42:21.338 --> 00:42:22.964
I love you.

00:42:25.383 --> 00:42:27.009
Love you too.

00:42:57.069 --> 00:42:58.862
You're too late.
